Z||000004||Shiner||03-16-2000||11:04 PM||||Boilermaker,<BR>I am restoring a GT almost EXACTLY like yours!  My paint doesn't look as nice though, heh.  I have a little bit of front end damage even!  It's not bad at all, but I don't think the fascia will bolt on straight unless I fix it.  <P> I am painting mine all red (like an '88) with gold wheels.  How about you?  I think gold really does look quite nice, but it just isn't me, you know?  <P> Good luck with the car!||||reg||1
Z||000005||BOILERMAKER||03-17-2000||07:46 AM||||I think that I am going to paint the car the original color.  Now, I have already put the rear fascia on from an 87 GT that was black and the front fascia will be from a black SE (anybody have a front GT fascia?)<P>So now the question is "what is the real original color of the car?"  I have chosen gold just because I don't see a lot of gold fiero's around here.<P>The observation of this car is at the time: it's truly a purdue car (gold an black ... sorry Bengal, but you owe me a beer now)||||reg||1
